I am looking for a STANDARD which defines how UTC (Universal Time Coordinate)
may be represented in binary.  I am aware of the ISO 8601:1988 standard which
defines TEXT representation of UTC, but this is not what is needed.

OpenVMS (from Digital Equipment) has defined a 128-bit representation of UTC.
However, it is not clear to which standards (if any) this representation 
adheres. 

Can anyone identify:
	1) On which standards the OpenVMS 128-bit representation is based.
	2) Any other (non-VMS) implementations of binary representation of UTC.
	3) Any existing or draft standards which address binary 
	   representation of UTC.





